 "intro_zh": "斋浦尔位于印度西北部拉贾斯坦邦，由萨瓦伊·贾伊·辛格二世于 1727 年建立，城墙环绕。与该地区其他位于丘陵地带的城市不同，斋浦尔建在平原上，并根据吠陀建筑的网格规划建造。街道以连续的柱廊商业为特色，在中心相交，形成了称为 chaupar 的大型公共广场。沿着主要街道建造的市场、商店、住宅和寺庙都有统一的外观。这座城市的城市规划体现了古代印度教和早期现代莫卧儿王朝以及西方文化的思想交流。网格规划是西方盛行的模式，而不同城市区域的组织（chowkris）则参考了传统的印度教概念。这座城市旨在成为商业之都，至今仍保持着当地的商业、手工艺和合作传统。",
 "intro_zh_source": "machine_translation",
 "intro_en": "The walled city of Jaipur, in India’s north-western state of Rajasthan was founded in 1727 by Sawai Jai Singh II. Unlike other cities in the region located in hilly terrain, Jaipur was established on the plain and built according to a grid plan interpreted in the light of Vedic architecture. The streets feature continuous colonnaded businesses that intersect in the centre, creating large public squares called chaupars . Markets, shops, residences and temples built along the main streets have uniform facades. The city's urban planning shows an exchange of ideas from ancient Hindu and early modern Mughal as well as Western cultures. The grid plan is a model that prevails in the West, while the organization of the different city sectors (chowkris) refers to traditional Hindu concepts. Designed to be a commercial capital, the city has maintained its local commercial, artisanal and cooperative traditions to this day.",
 "intro_en_source": "unesco_official",
